@@ -110,7 +110,11 @@
 
 The adapter uses HTTPX and an **OpenAI-compatible non-streaming `chat/completions`** endpoint, not an official provider SDK. It appends `/chat/completions` to the configured base URL. It asks for JSON text but does **not** assume provider JSON-mode support. Compatibility depends on the provider accepting this request and returning `choices[0].message.content` as a string. No specific provider URL or model is endorsed.
 
-Data is sent only after an explicit explanation request with consent: the question and deterministic analysis context, including selected signal names, values, window records, and timing settings. Matched RTL snippets are included only with separate RTL consent; this is not a full-project upload. Review proprietary or sensitive signal names and questions before sharing them.
+Data is sent only after an explicit explanation request with consent: the question and deterministic analysis context, including selected signal names, values, up to 128 window records per signal, strictly earlier/later neighboring records, and manually configured clock/reset names and settings. The analysis window is centered on the cursor and can differ from the visible viewport; neighboring records may lie outside it. The UI shows the actual analysis window. Matched RTL snippets (at most 32 name matches, up to 300 characters per line) are included only with separate RTL consent; this is not a full-project upload. These snippets can omit control flow or sampling rules. Review sensitive signal names and questions before sharing them.
+
+For a separately authorized first two-call acceptance session, set `AI_MAX_ATTEMPTS=1` and `AI_REQUEST_BUDGET=2` in the backend environment before startup. Otherwise the default is at most two HTTP attempts, with no process budget unless configured. Retries, timeouts and cancellations consume the optional budget; `/api/health` exposes `provider_http_attempts` separately from logical `requests`. The cap resets when the provider/backend restarts and is not a persistent billing or consent system: keep a separate acceptance ledger across restarts and do not resume merely by restarting. Configuration alone is not permission to send data. Cancellation cannot retract data or guarantee that a third party stops processing or billing.
+
+The live provider is **not verified**. A pure offline preparation command is available: `.venv/bin/python scripts/prepare_ai_evaluation.py --output <new-evidence.json>`. It preserves the original 18 content questions plus N1 Mock-only fault contract and adds explicit A1 asynchronous-reset coverage; answers and scores stay empty until real execution. It never reads provider configuration or calls a model. See the [current AI acceptance report](docs/qa/real-ai-acceptance-report.md).
 
 Responses undergo structural validation; signal/code references are checked against provided allowlists, and `observed_facts` is overwritten with backend-generated facts. **Free-text explanations can still hallucinate.** A valid response is neither a simulation result nor formal verification. Provider failures do not remove offline functionality. See [API](docs/api.md) and [limitations](docs/limitations.md).
 
